 "why": "D41 (KeZ north looking S from the fork, shops closed): openings ~2.2-3 m x 2.8-3.2 m under flat steel lintels, multi-leaf panelled steel doors (4-6 leaves) painted grey, beige and olive (atlas door_olive, the multi-leaf cell) and grey roll-downs, no teal or green; raised stone thresholds 0.15-0.2 m; corrugated canopies from both sides over the open bays; white hanging boards. Right side of D41 at 30-55 m from the camera, too far to read single doors: the colours follow the nearer KeZ doors in D41 (assumption). OSM shop nodes in this row: shoes x2, clothes 'Dakkak' (44 Beit HaBad St), confectionery, jewellery (5832848063/67/76/83, 5832849093). Bays start 9.8 m from the S end, where the sector boundary and the s04 infill begin; the canopy is one stepped awning per bay over the shops only, so no sheet runs over the blank south end into the s04 infill in front of it.",
